What does the program print?

```c
void swap(int *p, int *q) { *p = *p + *q; *q = *p - *q; *p = *p - *q; }
int main(void) {
    int v[3] = {4, 7, 9};
    swap(&v[0], &v[2]);
    swap(&v[1], &v[1]);
    printf("%d %d %d", v[0], v[1], v[2]);
    return 0;
}
```

For a real x and a large n, what does `s` approximate?

```c
double s = 0, t = x;
for (int i = 1; i <= n; i++) {
    s += t;
    t = -t * x * x / ((2 * i) * (2 * i + 1));
}
```
